You will see that the variance for this factor is negative and the p-value is not significant. That is why I constrain the variance to be 0. I am not sure whether it is correct or not.

The " psychological involvement, behavioral engagement, copresence, cohesion" are factors in first-order CFA. Also, the factor "social presence" is defined by the three factors "psychological involvement, behavioral engagement, and copresence", which forms a second-order CFA with no indicators.

In this case, I don't know whether the small sample size is the only reason for non-convergence. If it is not, what other possible reasons might be? And how to fix it?

