> Error in sim(1000, mod, n = 200, generate = x, lavaanfun = "cfa",  :
>   Please specify an appropriate object for the 'generate' argument: simsem model template, lavaan script, lavaan parameter table, OpenMx object, a list of options for the 'simulateData' function, or a function that takes sample size and provides data as an output.
>
> Any help would be much appreciated!

The error message seems pretty clear, and you can find information about those different "generate" methods on the ?sim help page.  For instance, if you want to use the simulateData() function, instead of calling that function with the arguments, you can save the list of arguments to pass to the "generate" argument:

> simArgs <- list(model = popModel, sample.nobs = 200, skewness = 1.5, kurtosis = 6)
> Output1 <- sim(..., generate = simArgs)

You should exclude the "seed" argument because that would mean all 1000 replications would generate the same data set.  Instead, you should use the "seed" argument in the sim() function.  Also, notice the ?sim help page says you can specify the distributions of indicators using the "indDist" argument, so you could also specify the skew/kurtosis using the bindDist() function.

